      "domain": "numpy.org",
      "rank": 1
    },
    {
      "title": "Coefficient of Variation (CV) in Python with NumPy",
      "url": "https://realpython.com/python-coefficient-of-variation/",
      "snippet": "The coefficient of variation is calculated as `CV = standard deviation / mean`, and is commonly expressed as a percentage by multiplying by 100. In NumPy, `np.std(x, ddof=0)` returns the population standard deviation, which is the default setting used in many basic examples with data like `x = [10, 12, 23, 23, 16, 23, 21, 16]`.",
      "domain": "realpython.com",
      "rank": 2
    },
