      "snippet": "Python 3.12 documentation explains that pstdev() returns the population standard deviation of sample data, using the population formula with denominator n rather than n-1. The mean() function is also defined in the same module, making it a standard reference for calculating coefficients of variation from mean and standard deviation.",
      "domain": "docs.python.org",
      "rank": 2
